            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="0909" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/4529a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Beirut</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Palmer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-08T18:00:00-04:00">July 8, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Please inform the Department regarding the French Fleet in your area,
                    including particularly the units present and the attitude of the officers and
                    men. Information is also desired regarding alleged fighting on the
                    Syrian-Palestine border, regarding an announced determination of the French
                    authorities to defend Syria “against any foreign encroachments”, and regarding
                    Weygand’s present activities and influence in Syria.</p>
                <p>Keep the Department advised by frequent short telegrams at least until the
                    Franco-British situation is clarified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
